1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,133
One raid. Three rounds. A reason to stay. A one-account test raid on babafesti, driven by real Twitch chat.

2
00:00:13,133 --> 00:00:23,133
Lower Third keeps the upper 70% of the stream visible. Counted moves show names and streaks; sound is opt-in.

3
00:00:23,133 --> 00:00:35,133
Judge mode: 300 simulated Raiders face 20 Home Guard. Participation rates make the final push count.

4
00:00:35,133 --> 00:00:47,633
Know Your Host uses A/B/C answers. This practice shows an authored fallback question.

5
00:00:47,633 --> 00:00:59,233
Fusion Boss turns opponents into teammates. Hit the shared boss; weak-point keywords deal triple damage.

6
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:10,833
Boss defeated in this one-account real-chat test. The end card invites both communities to follow.

7
00:01:10,833 --> 00:01:14,233
Afterglow: 1 recently active raider. One-account test.

8
00:01:14,233 --> 00:01:22,433
An unknown raid waits for the host. Trust next time takes effect only after successful acceptance.

9
00:01:22,433 --> 00:01:28,333
Enforced policy blocks an unfamiliar two-day-old account before the rumble starts.

10
00:01:28,333 --> 00:01:38,333
Separate hosted start: 1,475 ms. Signed evaluation and binding verified; receipt finalization timed out.

11
00:01:38,333 --> 00:01:48,333
One Codex chat. AGENTS.md defines pure plug-in rounds: start, onInput, tick and result.

12
00:01:48,333 --> 00:01:58,333
Genuine Codex app capture: three subagents working during the enhancement pass.

13
00:01:58,333 --> 00:02:06,333
The original three rounds were built concurrently. Timestamped task records document their shared overlap.

14
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:12,333
609 tests across 71 files. Attribution, fairness, spam limits, grants and all four scenarios verified.

15
00:02:12,333 --> 00:02:22,333
Full Arena is optional. Both communities win together, then discover each other through the follow invitations.

16
00:02:22,333 --> 00:02:29,333
Try it without accounts: pnpm i, then pnpm dev. github.com/ocularminds/raidrumble
